UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 1402(a), sole proprietorship net income of $300,000 is fully subject to self-employment tax at 15.3%. In an S corporation under Sec. 1366, only the $100,000 salary is subject to FICA under Sec. 3121. The $200,000 of pass-through income avoids employment taxes, saving approximately $200,000 x 15.3% = $30,600.
Wrong (A): There is a significant difference. The sole proprietorship subjects all $300,000 to SE tax, while the S corporation subjects only $100,000 in wages to FICA.
Wrong (B): $15,300 would represent 15.3% of only $100,000, which is the tax on the salary portion. The savings come from the $200,000 that avoids SE tax.
Wrong (D): $45,900 would represent 15.3% of the full $300,000. This overstates the savings because the $100,000 salary is still subject to FICA in either structure.$EXPL$
