  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 162(a)(1), compensation is deductible only if reasonable in amount. The IRS will recharacterize the $200,000 excess over comparable pay as a constructive dividend, which is not deductible by the corporation. This creates double taxation on the excess amount.
Wrong (A): The IRS routinely challenges unreasonable compensation under Section 162(a)(1) and established case law. Compensation is not solely a business decision when it exceeds reasonable levels.
